course: dictionary
lesson: 5455
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at this: «To a wild animal a city is not concrete and cars, it is a strange new landscape.» Here the writer is describing a view of a place and everything in it, so landscape means the view of the land.
explain: Context also tells you what job a word does. In «a beautiful landscape», the word after landscape names a thing you can see. In «to landscape the garden», the word is an action, so it is a verb. Ask yourself what the word is doing in the sentence, then try your meaning in it and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In the animal sentence, «tall buildings are cliffs» and «railway banks are hedges» show that the writer is describing a place as if it were wild countryside. The clues tell you that landscape means the view, not a painting or a computer screen.
fact: Landscape means everything you can see across a wide area of land, such as hills, fields, rivers, trees and buildings.
fact: A landscape can also be a painting or photo of such a view.
fact: Landscape format means a page or screen that is wider than it is tall.
fact: To landscape a garden or park means to change its shape and plant things to make it look nicer.
fact: The landscape of something means its general situation, as in «the political landscape».
exercise: In «To a wild animal a city is... a strange new landscape», what does landscape mean? | A garden that has been planted | A computer screen turned sideways | *The view of the land and everything in it | A painting of a city
exercise: Mia's tablet screen is wider than it is tall. Which word describes this? | Portrait | Scenery | Landscaped | *Landscape
exercise: «The council will landscape the old park this summer.» What does landscape mean here? | Put a fence around the park | Paint a picture of the park | *Change its shape and plant things to make it look nicer | Count the trees in the park
test: «The political landscape changed after the election.» In this sentence, what does landscape mean? | *Its general situation | A wide field of grass | A map of the streets | A painting of the election
test: Which word means a page or screen that is wider than it is tall? | *Landscape | Scenery | Portrait | Landscaped
exam: Which sentence uses landscape as a verb? | The painting of the lake is a landscape | The walk took us over a wide landscape | Turn the phone into landscape mode | *We will landscape the back garden to add a pond
